/-!
# The concrete 55-matrix orbit for the Lyons alternating quotient

The 55 saved matrices are indexed by unordered pairs of eleven letters.
Their first four entries in row zero distinguish them. Kernel-checked
carry-free row products prove the two intertwining identities with the
literal outputs of ATLAS `LyG1-max4W1`. The published pair permutations
already invert GAP's right actions, matching left matrix conjugation.

This supplies `PairOrbitCertificate` unconditionally. The parent quotient
construction uses the eleven incidence stars to obtain its A₁₁ quotient;
no decomposition, rank, idempotence or group-order assertion is needed here.

Source: GLS3 section 5.3, Lyons involution table, printed p.278. Original
ATLAS matrices and attribution are in `Atlas111Source/` and
`Atlas111InvolutionSource/`; candidate discovery is in `source/`, and
reproducible Lean certificate generation in `PairOrbit/source/Generate.py`.
-/

namespace Lyons.SimplicityCertificate.AlternatingQuotient

